cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data or code, please cite the paper and this release."
title: "MSI-Bench: data and code for a credibility assessment and conflict-aware evidence fusion framework for multi-source maritime safety information"
type: dataset
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-14"
url: "https://github.com/open-msi-lab/msi-bench"
repository-code: "https://github.com/open-msi-lab/msi-bench"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  MSI-Bench is a semi-synthetic benchmark for credibility assessment and evidence
  fusion of multi-source maritime safety information under graded mimicry attacks. It
  couples 1,118 real NAVAREA IV navigational warnings (2022-2023) with a simulated
  crowdsourced, sensor and adversarial overlay. The release also contains the
  NAVAREA IV warning archive 2012-2024 (U.S. NGA, public domain), the reference
  implementation of the framework and of all experiments, and the frozen results
  reported in the paper.
keywords:
  - maritime safety information
  - navigational warnings
  - credibility assessment
  - Dempster-Shafer evidence theory
  - Sybil attack
  - benchmark
